  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:4163",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the regulation of 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase through a series of interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Theasaponin E1 acts as a target of K-252a, which in turn targets 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase. This indicates a potential regulatory pathway where Theasaponin E1 may influence the activity of 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase through K-252a. Additionally, Theasaponin E1 is also shown to target another protein, Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is also targeted by K-252a. While the exact mechanism by which Theasaponin E1 influences 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase remains unclear, the shared target of K-252a suggests a possible functional link between Theasaponin E1 and the enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of K-252a as a central mediator in the interaction between Theasaponin E1 and 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanism.",
